Excerpts from netnews.rec.games.hack: 26-Sep-93 Wands of cancellation:
any .. by Mark Nelson@betty.cis.ud 
> So, can anyone tell me, what good is a wand of cancellation?  The only use I
> can think of is getting rid of a curse in order to take off a cursed item,
> but doesn't zapping yourself with a wand of cancellation cancel all of your
> intrinsics?  That seems like a high cost to pay, except for for very early
> in the game.

First of all, one of the most common misperceptions about Nethack is
that wands of cancellations get rid of intrinsics.  They don't.  I've
used them to rid myself of cursed stuff before.  All you have to do is
make sure you get rid of all your cancellable stuff first by dropping
it.  The other major uses include turning potions and scrolls into water
and paper as well as rendering certain monsters harmless (like nymphs). 
I've never blown up a bag of holding either, since when I put wands into
a bag I make sure that I'm just putting in wands (so I don't get "y"-key
happy) and I'm very careful.  The other solutions include just not
putting wands in your bag at all and leaving wands of cancellation
behind (since monsters don't zap them at you, you won't get hurt by
them).

